# No LFS tracking in the parent repo. The previous install flow required
# GIT_LFS_SKIP_SMUDGE=1 on clone (to avoid pulling the eos/ submodule's
# 27 GB through LFS), which also left these small parent-repo data files
# as pointer stubs and triggered "could not convert string to float:
# 'version https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1'" at import time. Storing
# them as regular git objects (~62 MB total) eliminates the trap and
# saves LFS bandwidth on every clone. The eos/ submodule still uses
# LFS for its 27 GB of EOS tables; setup_eos.py fetches those from
# Zenodo instead, preserving the LFS bandwidth budget.

# Files excluded from `git archive` (Zenodo / release tarballs).
.gitattributes export-ignore
.gitignore     export-ignore
